eric prince the former navy seal and  founder of blackwater the infamous  military contractor that took on lots  and lots of work during the iraq and  afghanistan wars was recently on the  sean ryan show and he talked about  bitcoin cryptocurrencies the u.s dollar  and geopolitics there's a fascinating  conversation because this is an  individual who has immense amounts of  data and information at its fingertips  and he's also highly connected with  various global leaders around the world  in the conversation prince points out  that he believes that sanctions are  actually weakening the us dollar on a  global stage the u.s dollar is the  global reserve currency but he points  out that those financial sanctions  against russia and other countries are  actually incentivizing various countries  that are large and may not be as  friendly with the united states to come  together and start to do trade in a  bilateral way without using the dollar  as that common unit of account now of  course eric prince sharing his own  personal opinions but it is fascinating  to hear him talk about what he calls  society level change with the united  states if they lose u.s dollar dominance  having to pay for many of their prior  errors here's exactly what eric had to  say about financial sanctions and the  potential diminishing power that the us  dollar may carry on that global stage so  for the last  70 years  we've enjoyed the dollar being the  world's reserve currency right and what  that allows  washington to do is spend trillions of  dollars extra part of the of the aura or  the the facade  of the the dollar being the world's  reserve currency is that there's this  american military hegemony right we have  this amazing military that can smack any  target anytime anywhere  and and when you have the debacle that  was afghanistan a failure in iraq a  failure of deterrence in ukraine when  that failure of deterrence now leads to  conflict between russia and ukraine and  now everybody goes  hog wild on sanctioning everything  russia right russia is still the largest  energy producer in the world they're  going to sell their stuff somewhere and  somebody's going to buy it right they  want to be paid in rubles yeah and  they'll trade with india  who can pay with rupees and the chinese  will pay with renminbi right so they  call it the three rs and so they create  a trading block to further reduce  the the hegemony that the dollar has in  trade  when when the dollar loses that status  then our idiots in washington's can't  spend an extra trillion dollars a year  and when america has to finally live  within its means and start to pay that  debt back  holy [ __ ] that is  that is society transforming level  change now when you hear eric prince  talk about these things the first  question i have well what exactly would  this future look like if the financial  sanctions actually do weaken the us  dollar and later in the conversation  with sean ryan prince lays out that  weimar germany which is decades-old  story could be a cautionary tale the  united states should pay attention to  here's prince describing why germany is  so important to understand as we move  forward in this current monetary policy  regime you took a country like germany  that lost world war one  and they printed and printed and printed  money  and the mighty  history of the german prussian society  collapsed  and all that wealth was destroyed  because it went from  you know one mark one german mark to buy  a loaf of bread  up to  a billion marks  to buy a loaf of bread just  hyperinflation that ran away  and the german society elected  a psychopath like adolf hitler  and that's the that's the kind of  insanity we have to prevent  now of course  eric prince myself and anyone else who's  watching this has no clue what's going  to happen in the future but to  understand the intricacies and the  complexities that revolve on the  geopolitical stage when you add in  central banks monetary policy and  various other issues it all becomes  clear that we could be headed towards  some pretty bumpy times now one of the  weird things in the bitcoin community is  that the more you understand the legacy  system the more you realize that we need  a new system there's lots of issues and  eventually those issues will come to a  head  now i don't like the doomsday stuff i  actually am a deep deep optimist i  believe that we live in the greatest  time in human history it's the most  prosperous and safest time  and i hope that we have a better future  than our past but i also understand that  you have to be rational you have to take  an honest look where are we headed and  what can we do to mitigate the risks  as we continue to see the geopolitical  stage unfold listening to someone like  eric prince even though he's  controversial even though many people  disagree with some of his actions or  previous things he said it's important  as i mentioned he's got immense amounts  of information at his fingertips and  he's very well connected on the global  stage with leaders people of power and  influence watching this interview was  eye-opening for me and to hear him talk  about financial sanctions weakening the  us dollar dominance and potentially  leading or contributing to  hyperinflation in the u.s  it's not something that's guaranteed  something that i hope never happens but  it's something that we should understand  we should pay attention to and we should  encourage our leaders to do everything  they possibly can to mitigate that risk
 

